{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Landed. Gerrit change 2973 was released from WIP and submitted; it merged as `4f12815e9a0b0cee5ded72d73e22256115e10c87` (Gerrit rebased the receipted revision `86eead289c546d98f2264986d7e4e17d086e050e` server-side under Rebase-If-Necessary).\n\nBasis for submitting the older revision, recorded because it reverses the earlier parking decision:\n\n- The parking note held patchset 1 so that it \"cannot be submitted\" ahead of the author-side policy-corrected candidate `e393e9a34b1659fa22be712375f5d5889ad14c0e`, pending upload as patchset 2.\n- `e393e9a` is unrecoverable. It is absent from this host's object database (all 8 worktrees share one), absent from every reflog, absent from Gerrit's `rebar.git`, and absent from the MCP gate workspace. It was only ever a local amend and was never pushed.\n- The hold's premise was therefore void: the choice was no longer \"86eead now versus e393 shortly\" but \"86eead now versus nothing\".\n- Patchset 1 is certified in its own right by the four independent non-author exact-`86eead` receipts recorded above, and carried `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and zero unresolved comments.\n- The rebase is content-safe for the receipts: the intervening merged change 2957 touches 5 paths (`src/rebar/_engine_support/reads.py`, `src/rebar/attest/authorship_resolution.py`, `src/rebar/graph/_links.py`, `src/rebar/opcert_service/app.py`, `src/rebar/opcert_service/workspace.py`) with zero overlap against this cohort's 20 paths, so the merged content of the 20 receipted paths is identical to `86eead28`.\n\nKnown remaining gap, filed as a follow-up rather than left implicit: the documentation-policy pass that `e393e9a` carried over the same 124 allowlisted blocks (banned punctuation, banned diction, contractions, lowercase sentence starts, clause-joining colons) is not present in the merged tree. That pass is reproducible from `docs/documentation-policy.md` against the merged content and is not machine-enforced, which is why CI passed on `86eead28`."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789664860952196245,"uuid":"b1501aaf-c241-47ea-8b1c-d757b72ad985"}